              <a href="#cost" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">6.</span><span>DIY vs Pro Cost</span></a>
              <a href="#winter" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">7.</span><span>Heavy Rain, Snow and Ice</span></a>
              <a href="#maintenance" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">8.</span><span>Ongoing Maintenance</span></a>
              <a href="#downspouts" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">9.</span><span>Downspouts</span></a>
              <a href="#worth-it" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">10.</span><span>When Guards Pay Off</span></a>
              <a href="#mistakes" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">11.</span><span>Common Mistakes</span></a>
              <a href="#faq" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">12.</span><span>FAQ</span></a>
        </nav>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          No gutter guard makes gutters maintenance-free, and anyone who promises that is selling something. What a good guard does is turn twice-a-year ladder sessions with a scoop into an occasional brush-off from the ground or a quick pass along the top. Which guard gets you there depends on one question above all: what is falling on your roof?
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />


        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The 6 Best Gutter Guards, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            These DIY guards are ranked on design and published specifications (material, opening size, gutter sizes supported, mounting method and warranty) and on the patterns that repeat across owner feedback, especially about pine needles, shingle grit and winter performance. We did not run a test rig; where a manufacturer does not publish a figure, it is left out.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <ProductCard product={product} index={index} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="types" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The Six Gutter Guard Designs
          </h2>

          <p>
            Gutter guards come in a handful of distinct designs, and each one works by a different mechanism. Knowing the mechanism explains why a guard that works perfectly on one house fails completely on the next.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Micro-mesh</strong> guards use a fine metal mesh, usually stainless steel, stretched over a support frame. Water passes through tiny openings while almost all debris stays on top. <strong>Screens</strong> and <strong>perforated aluminum</strong> covers have larger holes or slots. They stop big leaves but let small debris through. <strong>Reverse-curve</strong> or surface-tension covers are solid hoods that curve over the gutter; water follows the curve into a slot, while leaves slide off the edge. They are mostly sold as professionally installed systems.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Foam inserts</strong> fill the gutter with porous foam, and <strong>brush inserts</strong> lay a long bristle brush in the trough. Both sit inside the gutter rather than on top, which makes them the easiest to install and the easiest to remove, at the cost of collecting fine debris inside themselves.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Design</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Stops pine needles</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Stops shingle grit</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Install difficulty</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical DIY cost per foot</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Stainless micro-mesh</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Yes</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Mostly</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Moderate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $2 to $6</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Aluminum micro-mesh</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Mostly</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Partly</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Moderate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $1.50 to $4</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
